  "prefLabel": "Occ 102.06 Occupational therapy assistant (OTA)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Occ 102.06 “Occupational therapy assistant (OTA)” means “occupational therapy assistant” as defined in RSA 326-C:1, III, namely, “a person currently licensed to assist in the practice of occupational therapy, under the supervision of an occupational therapist, in the state of New Hampshire.”\n\nSource. #14366, eff 9-9-25 (from Occ 102.04)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/occ100-500.html"
